{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"4f1686630d054a8e","name":"card_event_observer_corps","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/WorldAtWar/events/card_event_observer_corps","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"OBSERVER CORPS","text":"Choose a card with cost 5 or more in your hand. Reduce its cost by 2.","flavorText":"The Observer Corps was an organization that was active from 1925 to 1995 and acted as the “Eyes and Ears” of the Royal Air Force (RAF). The members of the organization were mainly volunteers that were trained in aircraft recognition and their role was to spot enemy aircraft flying inland and to estimate their height and formation. This information was then used by the Fighter Command's operations to intercept the attacking formations. During WWII some 30,000 members of the Observer Corps were on active duty and control centers and observation posts across the UK were manned continuously, from 3 September 1939 to 12 May 1945, four days after VE day. The organization played a crucial role during the Battle of Britain, and in recognition for its services it became the Royal Observer Corps in 1941.","faction":"Britain","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_observer_corps","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_observer_corps_title","SourceString":"OBSERVER CORPS","LocalizedString":"OBSERVER CORPS"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_observer_corps_text","SourceString":"Choose a card with cost 5 or more in your hand. Reduce its cost by 2.","LocalizedString":"Choose a card with cost 5 or more in your hand. Reduce its cost by 2."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_observer_corps_history","SourceString":"The Observer Corps was an organization that was active from 1925 to 1995 and acted as the “Eyes and Ears” o